  "articleBody": "Investing in finished garage walls, improved lighting, and storage systems makes everyday life significantly easier. However, treating garage interiors like standard indoor drywall jobs without addressing durability leads to peeling finishes and damaged walls.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid:\n- Covering damp concrete or framing: Installing drywall over unaddressed water infiltration traps moisture, resulting in hidden rot and compromised drywall tape.\n- Undersizing electrical capacity: Running heavy workshop tools, extra freezers, or chargers on shared existing circuits trips breakers. Plan dedicated circuits before closing walls.\n- Extending house HVAC ducts: Pushing home heating ducts directly into the garage violates safety codes and pulls vehicle exhaust into your living quarters.\n- Forgetting wall blocking: Hanging heavy cabinetry or wall storage racks into unsupported drywall causes pulled anchors. Install structural backing between studs first.\n- Neglecting the house-to-garage fire door: Failing to seal the adjoining access door compromises fire safety and energy efficiency for the entire home.\n\nAvoiding these pitfalls requires practical trade knowledge. HH Remodeling LLC handles interior framing, drywall, and finish carpentry with dependable on-site oversight. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your garage interior renovation today.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
